ch": "A late debate moment or data-center/affordability controversy could tighten the race, though Hull's fundraising shortfall limits his ability to capitalize.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Michelle Lujan Grisham (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New Mexico's open governor's race pits Democrat Deb Haaland against Republican Gregg Hull to succeed term-limited Michelle Lujan Grisham. Haaland has raised over $11 million to Hull's under $500,000, giving her a decisive advertising and organization edge. Polls from August show her ahead by margins ranging from a narrow 3 points to a wide 17, with averages clustering near 8-11 points.\n\nExpert raters overwhelmingly place the race in the Solid or Likely Democratic column, and prediction markets price Haaland's chances around 93-95 percent. The state's modest Democratic lean and the open-seat dynamic keep some uncertainty, but Hull faces an uphill climb with limited resources and little evidence of a competitive race developing.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9664, "margin": 10.58}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9571, "margin": 10.0}]}